    <string name="ca_btn_recheck">Re-check installation</string>
    <string name="ca_instructions">How to install (Android 11+):\nSettings › Security &amp; privacy › More security settings › Encryption &amp; credentials › Install a certificate › CA certificate → pick Download/OneProxyClick_CA.crt.\n(The legacy installer intent only shows a hint on Android 11+.)\n\nNotes:\n• Since Android 7 apps trust user CAs only if they opt in (network_security_config) or are debuggable builds you control. Chrome trusts user CAs; Firefox needs \"Use third party CA certificates\".\n• Apps with certificate pinning will fail the handshake: they appear in history as \"Client TLS handshake failed\". Add those hosts to the pass-through list in Settings.\n• Browsers can also fetch the cert from http://127.0.0.1:&lt;port&gt;/cert while the proxy is running.</string>
